Given the following Java source file, decide whether attacker-controlled data from a configured source can reach a configured sink without an adequate restriction (e.g. path normalization, allow-listing, a containment check) somewhere on the way. Respond with ONLY a JSON object, no prose outside it, in this exact shape:
{"findings": [{"cwe": "CWE-22", "class": "EnclosingClassName", "method": "methodName", "explanation": "one paragraph naming exactly where the missing or inadequate check is"}]}
List one finding per enclosing method you believe is actually responsible for the unguarded flow (there may be more than one, e.g. an entry method and a helper it calls). Use the class's simple name (no package) and the method name as written (for a constructor, use the class name). If you conclude every such flow is fully restricted, or no configured source reaches a configured sink across the file(s) shown, return {"findings": []}.

